{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789225666,"nonce":"oP6iwnB9PE5TJRx2CYpNQAK6aN0=","message":"Root cause: the two convert_type copies disagree on String. lowering.rs lowers PrimitiveType::String to Ptr(U8) (so every function declared to return str has a *u8 signature) while ssa.rs lowers it to Ptr(I8), which is what string literals are and the only pointer type the dynamic-box tagging reads as String. With ZYNTAX_DISABLE_INTERP_OPTS=1 the call result carries the SSA's *i8 and prints right; with inlining on, the inlined body's return value carries the signature's *u8 and boxes as Pointer.\n\nFix: lowering.rs lowers String to Ptr(I8), matching ssa.rs.","files":null}]}